-/// it, is a bend round a hole ring ([`Branches`], [`Walls::ring_near`]).
-///
-/// - **Why this set.** A node whose path does not bend sees the seed
-///   centre `c`, so its pivot is the seed and `ρ = R + T` exactly: the
-///   curvature law ([`curvature_levels`]) is derived for that circle and
-///   holds there without error. Where the path bends at a node `b` the
-///   front is a circle about `b`: `T = |b - c| - R + |x - b|`, so
-///   `(R + T) - |x - b| = |b - c|` (more bends only add to it), the
-///   distance from the seed to the bend node, which is never 0. So the
-///   law's `ρ` and the local `ρ` disagree at every zone node, and the set
-///   does not depend on a tolerance. A bend round the outer wall only (a
-///   lobe behind an inside corner) is left out: no two fronts meet there
-///   (one branch, C2), and the shipped shapes have none (the pocket's
-///   outer wall is convex; the seed sees the whole star). The meeting line
-///   lies in the zone: the two branches that meet there both went round
-///   the island.
-/// - **Closed off.** The zone is bounded by the island, the walls and the
-///   two shadow lines, the rays from the seed that touch the island. A ray
-///   from the seed is a gradient line of `T`, so the first region's wraps
-///   (circles about the seed) meet the border at a right angle, as at a
-///   wall: the last step of a wrap at the border meets only its band (the
-///   disc of the wrap below ends on the same ray and covers the stock on
-///   the inner side).
-/// - Not chosen: "the nodes of the second branch" (both branches reach the
-///   meeting line at the same `T`, by its definition, so "second" is an
-///   order of cutting, not a property of the field); "the nodes where the
-///   two `ρ` disagree by more than a tolerance" is this set, since the
-///   smallest disagreement is the seed's distance to the island.
-fn far_side_zone(field: &GeodesicField, walls: &Walls<'_>) -> Vec<bool> {
